From fca653ba38961d6bce1c20416b16d4ee1efad7c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:17:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 50/57] Z 6III: the body IMU -- gyro, FIFO and timestamps, and
 a settable I2C rate

nikon-z63-imu.h gains the gyro side of the posture sensor: its FIFO,
timestamps and byte order as the firmware reads them, so the stock image
now sees a real 1 g. -machine imu-dps= sets the rotation (default a slow
sine), imu-clock-ppm= the sensor's clock error, and i2c-byte-ns= the time
an I2C byte takes on the EXPEED's banks (nikon-z63-i2c.h; default about
24 us, the driver's divisors at an unmeasured 100 MHz pclk). Bus steps
catch up in virtual time instead of drifting.

Pass -machine imu-mg=-1000:0:0 for a level body: the old default of 1 g
on Z puts the GUI into its rotated layout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
